# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recorded and derived data. This is the important one.
#
# data/live/books.jsonl alone is ~43 GB, data/uniform ~13 GB and
# data/viewer_full ~13 GB. GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB and
# warns past a ~5 GB repo, so none of this can be committed. All of it is
# reproducible from the recorder output; only the small MLB Stats API window
# file is worth keeping in the repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/game_windows.json

# Analysis OUTPUTS are small and worth versioning -- they are the findings,
# not bulk data. 4 MB total: the per-event CSV, the figures, and the cached
# aggregate arrays (which stand in for ~25 minutes of recomputation).
!data/collapse/
!data/collapse/**

# Generated viewer page (rebuild with build_viewer_multi.py; it embeds the
# manifest from data/viewer_full/index.json, so it churns on every rebuild).
viewer_full.html

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# Logs and scratch
*.log

# Unattended run logs
logs/
